---
/**
 * Footer — colophon, the outbound link cluster, and the copyright line.
 *
 * ADR-0004: this is a direct child of <body>, a sibling of <main>, so it maps
 * to the `contentinfo` landmark. Phase 0's "six headings inside one main"
 * criterion is superseded for this component, and the placeholder <h2> is gone
 * rather than reworded: docs/copy.md §Footer specifies a colophon, a link set
 * and a copyright line — no heading — and ADR-0003 forbids inventing copy to
 * fill one. A body-level <footer> needs no accessible name. Headings on the
 * page are now one h1 and four h2s, all inside <main>, levels unbroken.
 *
 * Copy is rendered verbatim from docs/copy.md §Footer (ADR-0003). Strings sit
 * on ONE source line so the built output greps literally against the deck
 * (convention from phase-1-ws-1.1), with the two exceptions the deck itself
 * forces:
 *
 *   - The colophon ends in a markdown link, `[Read the audit trail](…)`. A
 *     functional link has to be a real <a>, so the string splits there and
 *     nowhere else — the sentence before it, the label, and the trailing "."
 *     are each still byte-for-byte deck text, and the period sits OUTSIDE the
 *     anchor because that is where the deck puts it.
 *   - "**Links:** GitHub · Docs · Releases · MIT License" is a spec, not a
 *     rendered string: it names four links and their order, and four anchors
 *     can never be one text node. Same category as §Protocol's "Diagram states
 *     (in order)" line, which phase-1-ws-1.3 treated as structural. The <ul>
 *     carries the order and the interpuncts are decorative CSS, exactly as
 *     1.3's connectors are. Grep units are the four labels.
 *
 * The colophon's claim is literally true and the link is its evidence: every
 * section of this page was dispatched, briefed, coded and cross-vendor
 * reviewed as a slice, and github.com/techspeque/metiswww carries the ledger.
 *
 * "MIT License" is the one link the deck gives no URL for. It points at
 * metis's LICENSE (verified 200, and its content is the MIT text); this
 * repository has no LICENSE of its own, and the other three links all point at
 * the metis repo, so pointing this one anywhere else would be the odd choice.
 *
 * `©` and `·` are literal characters, never entities — dist has to stay
 * entity-free for the deck to grep against literal bytes (1.3's evidence).
 *
 * The container rules below duplicate index.astro's <main> rules on purpose.
 * Astro scopes styles to the elements in their own template, so once the
 * footer is a sibling rather than a descendant, index.astro's `main` rule
 * cannot reach it — and without the inline padding the footer text would sit
 * flush against the viewport edge while every section above it is inset.
 */
---

<footer class="footer">
  <p class="colophon">Built by AI agents, governed by metis — every section of this page was planned, coded, and cross-vendor reviewed as a slice in its own ledger. <a
      href="https://github.com/techspeque/metiswww"
      rel="noopener">Read the audit trail</a>.</p>

  <ul class="links" role="list">
    <li><a href="https://github.com/techspeque/metis" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/techspeque/metis/tree/main/docs" rel="noopener">Docs</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/techspeque/metis/releases" rel="noopener">Releases</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://github.com/techspeque/metis/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener"
        >MIT License</a
      >
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="copyright">© 2026 techspeque</p>
</footer>

<style>
  /* Mirrors index.astro's <main> container — see the frontmatter for why it is
     repeated rather than inherited. */
  .footer {
    max-width: var(--container-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    padding-inline: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  /* Muted on base: 8.39:1 dark, 5.66:1 light (tokens.css ratio table). The
     audit-trail link inherits the global anchor colour — accent on base,
     8.17:1 dark / 5.53:1 light. Both AA. */
  .colophon {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* Order lives in the markup, so the separators can be decorative. role="list"
     is explicit because `list-style: none` makes WebKit drop the list role
     (f-005), and that role is what lets the interpuncts be decoration. */
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    /* Also the row gap once the cluster wraps on a narrow viewport. */
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    /* Drops the UA list indent — the token zero, not a raw 0 (f-003). */
    padding: var(--space-0);
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* The interpunct the deck draws between labels. Decorative: it separates
     items the flex gap and the list role already separate, so nothing is lost
     when it is unstyled or unseen. It hangs off the PRECEDING item, not the
     following one, which is what makes it wrap correctly: as part of that
     item's box it can only ever end a line — the familiar "continues below"
     separator — where a leading ::before would start a wrapped row with a
     stray mark that reads as a bullet. Its margin plus the flex gap put equal
     space on either side, so it sits centred between two labels. */
  .links li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: "·";
    margin-inline-start: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .copyright {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
</style>
